==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|allodial}}, and its source, {{der|en|la|allodialis||held in freehold}}, from {{m|la|allodium}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} Pertaining to [[land]] owned by someone [[absolutely]], without any [[feudal]] obligations; held without acknowledgement of any superior. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#*'''2016''', {{w|Peter H. Wilson}}, ''The Holy Roman Empire'', Penguin 2017, p. 351:
#*:Henry reconciled the Zähringer, whom he had deposed from Carinthia in 1078, by raising their '''allodial''' property in the Black Forest to a new duchy 20 years later.

